{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NxFNc7VHKoCDVAnpBymE97","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"The Apache Kafka JIRA issue that tracks KIP-1307 \\\\\\\"SerDe and Interceptor Metrics\\\\\\\" is **KAFKA-20386**.\\\\n\\\\nSupporting facts, in time order:\\\\n\\\\n- **2026-03-31T21:50:08.000000Z** - KAFKA-20386 was created by Aditya Kousik with summary \\\\\\\"SerDe and Interceptor Metrics\\\\\\\", status Open, priority Major, components clients, consumer, producer. [jira:13646867:created]\\\\n- **2026-03-31T21:50:52.599000Z** - The issue's description was updated by Aditya Kousik to append \\\\\\\"See [KIP-1307|https://cwiki.apa…\\\\\\\" (the KIP-1307 cwiki link), explicitly tying the issue to KIP-1307. [jira:13646867:change:23002903:0]\\\\n- **2026-03-31T21:51:00.000000Z** - A JIRA creation notification email was sent by \\\\\\\"Aditya Kousik (Jira)\\\\\\\" with subject \\\\\\\"  (KAFKA-20386) SerDe and Interceptor Metrics\\\\\\\", confirming the issue key, summary, and components. [mail:ae3afc9065b1b455fcfba134]\\\\n- **2026-04-01T15:34:12.000000Z** - Aditya Kousik started the mailing list discussion \\\\\\\" KIP-1307: SerDe and Interceptor Metrics\\\\\\\", referencing the same KIP-1307 cwiki page and the same problem statement (missing client-side metrics for serialization, deserialization, and interceptors). [mail:3a486f07414ee44d7163c381]\\\\n- **2026-04-16T19:17:20.000000Z** - Aditya Kousik posted a follow-up to the same discussion thread, referencing the KIP-1307 discussion and a March 2026 Monthly Digest summary. [mail:762e9120bdb64c23c73d6106]\\\\n\\\\nAll findings agree that KAFKA-20386 is the issue tracking KIP-1307; the description update and mailing list posts occurred after the issue's creation and confirm the connection.\\\\n\\\\nWhat could not be determined: Nothing - the findings consistently identify KAFKA-20386 as the tracking issue, and no conflicting issue was found.\\\",\\\"erro